A||||9||Rare87GT||Eibach Lowering Springs Questions||||1||
Z||000000||Rare87GT||12-22-2001||01:17 PM||||For the people that have them, how is the ride compared to stock?  Is it very bouncy or does it ride about the same as stock does?  I know the ride will be stiffer and such but I was hoping it didn't bounce like the ricers do.  And if you do have eibach's how much of a drop have you gone with them.  And lastly is there a lot of difference in coilovers and drop spindles compared to just getting eibach's in front and back?  People that have Eibach's where did you buy them and how much did they cost?  Thank you.<P>------------------<BR>1987 GT (Maroon)*5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000001||sluppy123||12-22-2001||01:26 PM||||I've got a set of Eibach sport springs on my 87' GT. The ride is a bit stiffer than stock, but is dosen't bounce all over the road. If you really want a stiff ride buy a set of Intrax springs, IMO they really suck on a Fiero, Way to stiff and it bounces all over the road.<P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>87' GT- Turbo Charged, Modified 2.8- 235 HP w/ 7 psi Boost,<BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1711832&a=12781563&p=54316496&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Howard_Sacks||12-22-2001||01:43 PM||||I haven't driven on mine yet but they only cost $185 from shox.com when I bought them with kyb shocks and struts.  Total was under $400 shipped. <P>Howard<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rare87GT||12-22-2001||02:13 PM||||sluppy123, how much were your set of Eibach springs and how much of a drop was it?  Where can I purchase Eibach's and KYB Struts/Shocks?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||12-22-2001||02:57 PM||||Eibachs don't bounce- it's more of a jolt.||||reg||1
