Z||000006||tgowens||12-22-2001||08:03 PM||||I have Eibach's on one of my GT's -- it is about a 1 1/2" drop and they do ride stiffer than stock springs. Not really stiff until I put that Herb Adams sway bar on the rear -- but -- good gosh does it ever hold the road!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rare87GT||12-23-2001||02:25 AM||||Where can I buy a new set of Eibach Lowering Springs so I can lower my car.  Do you know of a good website.  And is 1 1/2" the lowest I can drop it with Eibach's?  And where is a good place to get KYB Struts.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000008||btoth||12-23-2001||01:17 PM||||Fiero Store of course has them.  But you can find them at other places that sell suspension parts.  Probably for less $ too.||||reg||1
Z||000009||cadero2dmax||12-23-2001||01:24 PM||||Bounce is caused soft shocks. Even stock springs would bounce with no shocks, or weak, worn out ones.<P>Buy a good set of Kyb's or Konis, and go as stiff as you want with your springs.<P>G<BR>||||reg||1
